@tavojs/ui-core validates theme configuration and returns color ramps, semantic modes, static tokens, resolved breakpoints, and accessibility warnings as plain data. It has no DOM, component renderer, Tavo.js runtime, Vite, CSS module, or React Native dependency.

**Most web applications should not install this directly**

Use @tavojs/ui for web components, theme CSS, runtime theme controls, and the web CLI. UI Core is for custom renderers, design-token exporters, build tools, and platform-neutral pipelines.

[

## Resolve configuration

Learn required values, preset precedence, overrides, and validation behavior.Read guide →

](/docs/ui-core/config)[

## Install for custom tooling

Add the platform-neutral package and export a validated token artifact without importing web components.Read guide →

](/docs/ui-core/installation)[

## Generate tokens

Use the complete build result and emit platform-specific output.Read guide →

](/docs/ui-core/tokens)[

## Choose color behavior

Compare presets, methods, ramps, and exact action colors.Read guide →

](/docs/ui-core/presets-and-colors)[

## Enforce constraints

Resolve responsive thresholds and contrast warnings.Read guide →

](/docs/ui-core/breakpoints-and-accessibility)

**Create scripts/export-tokens.mjs**

```js
import { mkdir, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
import { buildThemeTokens } from "@tavojs/ui-core";

const theme = buildThemeTokens({
  color: {
    light: {
      primary: "#116a67",
      secondary: "#d86c3d",
    },
  },
  accessibility: {
    contrast: "AA",
    failOnViolation: false,
  },
});

const artifact = {
  schemaVersion: 1,
  breakpoints: theme.breakpoints,
  modes: {
    light: {
      ...theme.staticTokens,
      ...theme.modes.light.tokens,
    },
    dark: {
      ...theme.staticTokens,
      ...theme.modes.dark.tokens,
    },
  },
  warnings: theme.warnings,
};

await mkdir("dist", { recursive: true });
await writeFile(
  "dist/design-tokens.json",
  `${JSON.stringify(artifact, null, 2)}
`,
);

if (theme.warnings.length > 0) {
  console.error(theme.warnings.join("
"));
  process.exitCode = 1;
}
```

**Merge package.json**

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "tokens:export": "node scripts/export-tokens.mjs"
  }
}
```

color.light.primary is the only required theme value. UI Core derives a secondary anchor when it is omitted and produces a dark mode when no complete dark palette is supplied.

**Reference Reference snippet**

```ts
import type { TavoUiThemeConfig } from "@tavojs/ui-core";

const config: TavoUiThemeConfig = {
  color: { light: { primary: "#116a67" } }
};
```

resolveThemeConfig starts from internal defaults, applies the chosen preset, then deeply merges explicit project values. A preset is a starting point, never a lock on the final design.

**Reference Reference snippet**

```ts
import { resolveThemeConfig } from "@tavojs/ui-core";

const resolved = resolveThemeConfig({
  preset: "enterprise",
  color: { light: { primary: "#7c5cff" } },
  scale: { density: "spacious", shadow: 0.2 }
});
```

Here the enterprise preset supplies unspecified values, while spacious density and the explicit shadow override its scale choices.

buildThemeTokens is the main orchestration API. It returns light and dark color sets, static tokens, resolved breakpoints, the resolved config, and accessibility warnings in one deterministic value.

**Reference Reference snippet**

```ts
import { buildThemeTokens } from "@tavojs/ui-core";

const theme = buildThemeTokens({
  color: { light: { primary: "#116a67", secondary: "#d86c3d" } },
  accessibility: { contrast: "AA" }
});

console.log(theme.modes.light.tokens["color-primary-bg"]);
console.log(theme.staticTokens["radius-md"]);
console.log(theme.breakpoints.md);
console.log(theme.warnings);
```

UI Core deliberately does not write CSS. A web tool can join static and mode tokens into variables, while another renderer can map the same result into a typed theme object.

**Reference Reference snippet**

```ts
function toVariables(tokens: Record<string, string>, prefix = "tui") {
  return Object.entries(tokens)
    .map(([name, value]) => `--${prefix}-${name}: ${value};`)
    .join("
");
}

const lightVariables = toVariables({
  ...theme.staticTokens,
  ...theme.modes.light.tokens
});
```

**Do not duplicate the web emitter casually**

If the target is a normal Tavo.js website, @tavojs/ui and tavo-ui already own CSS generation, selectors, theme injection, and runtime mode behavior.

The public package includes normalization, conversion, ramp, luminance, readable-text, and contrast helpers. These are useful for inspectors and custom token tooling that must explain how a theme result was produced.

**Reference Reference snippet**

```ts
import {
  contrastRatio,
  generateColorRamp,
  normalizeHex,
  readContrastColor
} from "@tavojs/ui-core";

const primary = normalizeHex("#7C5CFF");
const ramp = generateColorRamp(primary, "analogous", true);
const text = readContrastColor(primary);
const ratio = contrastRatio(text, primary);
```

**Action colors remain exact**

Solid action backgrounds use the configured primary or secondary value. The generator chooses black or white action text based on contrast rather than silently shifting the brand anchor.

resolveThemeBreakpoints merges project overrides with defaults and always returns numeric sm, md, and lg values. UI packages can use the same result for component props, generated CSS variables, and stylesheet media-query helpers.

**Reference Reference snippet**

```ts
import { resolveThemeBreakpoints } from "@tavojs/ui-core";

const breakpoints = resolveThemeBreakpoints({
  color: { light: { primary: "#116a67" } },
  breakpoints: { md: 820 }
});

// { sm: 480, md: 820, lg: 1024 }
```

Breakpoints decide when a layout switches. Viewport configuration describes fluid root-size scaling between minimum and maximum widths. Resolve it separately when a renderer needs to generate clamp-based typography or size behavior.

**Reference Reference snippet**

```ts
import { resolveThemeViewport } from "@tavojs/ui-core";

const viewport = resolveThemeViewport({
  color: { light: { primary: "#116a67" } },
  viewport: { rootMin: 14, rootMax: 16, minWidth: 320, maxWidth: 960 }
});
```

Set accessibility.contrast to AA or AAA to evaluate important foreground and background pairs during generation. Warnings stay in the result by default so design tooling can display them alongside the affected theme.

**Reference Reference snippet**

```ts
const review = buildThemeTokens({
  color: { light: { primary: "#777777" } },
  accessibility: { contrast: "AAA", failOnViolation: false }
});

if (review.warnings.length) console.warn(review.warnings);
```

**Enforce in CI deliberately**

Set failOnViolation to true when theme changes must fail the build. Keep it false in interactive design tools that need to show incomplete work and explain every issue.

